{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 1914, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nYou are given two integer arrays, nums1 and nums2, both of length n, along with a positive integer k.\nFor each index i from 0 to n - 1, perform the following:\n\nFind all indices j where nums1[j] is less than nums1[i].\nChoose at most k values of nums2[j] at these indices to maximize the total sum.\n\nReturn an array answer of size n, where answer[i] represents the result for the corresponding index i.\n \nExample 1:\n\nInput: nums1 = [4,2,1,5,3], nums2 = [10,20,30,40,50], k = 2\nOutput: [80,30,0,80,50]\nExplanation:\n\nFor i = 0: Select the 2 largest values from nums2 at indices [1, 2, 4] where nums1[j] < nums1[0], resulting in 50 + 30 = 80.\nFor i = 1: Select the 2 largest values from nums2 at index [2] where nums1[j] < nums1[1], resulting in 30.\nFor i = 2: No indices satisfy nums1[j] < nums1[2], resulting in 0.\nFor i = 3: Select the 2 largest values from nums2 at indices [0, 1, 2, 4] where nums1[j] < nums1[3], resulting in 50 + 30 = 80.\nFor i = 4: Select the 2 largest values from nums2 at indices [1, 2] where nums1[j] < nums1[4], resulting in 30 + 20 = 50.\n\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: nums1 = [2,2,2,2], nums2 = [3,1,2,3], k = 1\nOutput: [0,0,0,0]\nExplanation:\nSince all elements in nums1 are equal, no indices satisfy the condition nums1[j] < nums1[i] for any i, resulting in 0 for all positions.\n\n \nConstraints:\n\nn == nums1.length == nums2.length\n1 <= n <= 10^5\n1 <= nums1[i], nums2[i] <= 10^6\n1 <= k <= n\n\n### Format: You will use the following starter code to write the solution to the problem and enclose your code within delimiters.\n```python\nclass Solution:\n    def findMaxSum(self, nums1: List[int], nums2: List[int], k: int) -> List[int]:\n        \n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 1999, "char_start": 1926, "quote": "Input:\n[4, 2, 1, 5, 3]\n[10, 20, 30, 40, 50]\n2\nOutput:\n[80, 30, 0, 80, 50]", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 1: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R4", "source": {"char_end": 2066, "char_start": 2011, "quote": "Input:\n[2, 2, 2, 2]\n[3, 1, 2, 3]\n1\nOutput:\n[0, 0, 0, 0]", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 2: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}], "request_sha": "e3aee09bfa3738d05e962c8bde343e14dc4baee50d26f1a3e083c28d5f622c2d", "stop": null}, "kind": "requirements", "prev": "e79fc6e3d4b653dc6fb01087507cb238fe1a1694a73ceb91fe840d5046446013", "seq": 2}
